# Clarify in one pass

When the user runs `/speckit-clarify`, collect every question this pass still needs answered and ask them in a single message. Wait for the answers before writing the spec.

- Scan the active spec once. Include every question whose answer changes behaviour, data, acceptance tests, or scope.
- Do not cap the set at 5. If more than 5 questions are needed, ask all of them in that same message.
- Number them. Each item starts with `**Question:**` and ends with `?`.
- Give options or a suggested short answer under that question. Mark one recommended choice.
- Do not send a second question after the user answers the first. Do not hide later questions for a follow-up turn.
- If a reply misses a number, ask only for the missing numbers. Do not add new questions in that follow-up.
- If nothing material is ambiguous, say so and ask nothing.

```text
❌ Ask question 1, wait, then reveal question 2
✅ Send every needed question together, including when there are more than 5, then update the spec after one reply
```
